<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell diesel for March 1-12.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell diesel for March 1-12.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 225-250,000 barrels of 0.3 percent sulphur diesel lifting March 1-12 from Kaoshiung, a company source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on February 18 and bids are valid until February 20.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold two 225,000-250,000-barrel cargoes for January 26-February 15 lifting at around $29.50 per barrel free-on-board kaoshiung.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
